      "writtenOn": "2026-04-02T01:57:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had planned to codegen buffers as char arrays, but should this be more like other decompose transforms and modify the variable to that type instead? It might require function specialization to do so since the auto-conversions in the validator wouldn\u0027t apply.",
      "revId": "e0fd18ddd629b40d1eead35e7c8175f20f1b2d0f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9fc7fa26_7f04e3ba",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/msl/writer/raise/decompose_buffer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002266
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-02T02:22:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then it hits me that specialization will need to happen at some point still even then.",
      "parentUuid": "ccb96fff_45f5ce18",
      "revId": "e0fd18ddd629b40d1eead35e7c8175f20f1b2d0f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e4b5ad8b_dbbc1b63",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/msl/writer/raise/decompose_buffer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-02T21:56:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think I fully understand all of the issues here yet, but after thinking about `arrayLength()` for a bit it does feel like changing the buffer type to be an `array\u003cu8\u003e` may be the best option (also commented on one of the tests with thoughts about it).\n\nThe specialization requirement is annoying. I did wonder if we could just run the DirectVariableAccess transform before this one. But I suppose it would need to be taught how to handle `bufferView` calls to propagate the offset/size, which is a big chunk of the work done here anyway so might not actually be easier in the end. Hmm.",
      "parentUuid": "9fc7fa26_7f04e3ba",
      "revId": "e0fd18ddd629b40d1eead35e7c8175f20f1b2d0f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec7125b3_e28e65bc",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/msl/writer/raise/decompose_buffer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002266
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-03T01:16:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I got around specialization by introducing some extra reinterprets (pointer offset calls with no offset). So specialization is not required.\n\nThe array lengths might just appear in WGSL now after a buffer view so there does need to be a solution for them where they are affected by size.\n\nTake a look at patchset 5.",
      "parentUuid": "e4b5ad8b_dbbc1b63",
      "revId": "e0fd18ddd629b40d1eead35e7c8175f20f1b2d0f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73723faf_78c97635",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/msl/writer/raise/decompose_buffer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002266
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-04T01:31:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PS7 lowers all buffers to uchar arrays. See if that is preferable. One question it raises is about the alignment we treat these buffers as having. Will a WG variable be guaranteed to have the right alignment? Do we need to do anything to ensure that alignment?\n\nCan always revert this PS, but then the alignment question moves the buffer type. I originally found this running through ModuleScopeVars where buffers don\u0027t have an alignment.\n\nThis might actually raise a spec question.",
      "parentUuid": "ec7125b3_e28e65bc",
      "revId": "e0fd18ddd629b40d1eead35e7c8175f20f1b2d0f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b748022c_73e699fa",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/msl/writer/raise/decompose_buffer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002266
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-04T01:34:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could add `alignas` attribute in MSL (see section 2.5 in the MSL spec). Might have to search for the highest alignment needed. I *think* it would only be needed for workgroup variables.",
      "parentUuid": "73723faf_78c97635",
      "revId": "e0fd18ddd629b40d1eead35e7c8175f20f1b2d0f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7ef7205_e85f1723",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/msl/writer/raise/decompose_buffer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-07T21:02:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At the moment we do all of our workgroup allocations for MSL via `setThreadgroupMemoryLength`, which AFAICT guarantees a 16-byte base alignment. I think that avoids the need for us to add explicit `[[align()]]` attributes for now, though if we ever switch to static allocations we would need to.",
      "parentUuid": "b748022c_73e699fa",
      "revId": "e0fd18ddd629b40d1eead35e7c8175f20f1b2d0f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
