      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-03T01:16:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It definitely needs handled and it\u0027s just a subset of the length of the buffer. A user gets a runtime array out of a bufferView call and then calls arrayLength on it. So we need to limit the size (if from a bufferArrayView) and adjust for the offset.",
      "parentUuid": "9eda5dcc_f0c4d49b",
      "revId": "e0fd18ddd629b40d1eead35e7c8175f20f1b2d0f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e18e4cc_62c1fbb1",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/msl/writer/raise/decompose_buffer_test.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-07T21:02:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But shouldn\u0027t the operand to the new `arrayLength` instruction be the original pointer (i.e. `arrayLength %gv` instead of `arrayLength %3`)? Because IIUC you should be getting the total length of the original buffer and then subtracting the offset right?",
      "parentUuid": "54c7d792_6f82a18f",
      "revId": "e0fd18ddd629b40d1eead35e7c8175f20f1b2d0f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
